@node Transient menu
@section Transient menu

@findex agent-log-menu

The command @code{agent-log-menu} opens a transient menu that arranges all @code{agent-log} commands in side-by-side columns: Open@comma{} Sync & AI@comma{} and Settings are always visible; a fourth Navigate column appears when the current buffer is in @code{agent-log-mode}.  The keybinding is @samp{?} in @code{agent-log-mode}.  The menu is also available globally via its autoload@comma{} so you can bind it to a key of your choice outside of @code{agent-log-mode}.

The Open column includes @code{agent-log-resume-session} (bound to @samp{s})@comma{} which opens the session displayed in the current log in the coding agent.  The Sync & AI column includes the @code{agent-log-search} command@comma{} bound to @samp{/}.

The Navigate column groups movement commands (@samp{n}@comma{} @samp{p} for stepping through turns)@comma{} section folding (@samp{TAB} to toggle at point@comma{} @samp{C} to collapse all@comma{} @samp{E} to expand all)@comma{} and buffer operations (@samp{G} to re-render@comma{} @samp{w} to copy the current turn).  Note that the collapse and expand commands are one-shot operations on the current buffer view; the persistent per-type visibility defaults (hidden@comma{} collapsed@comma{} visible) are controlled by the Settings toggles (@samp{-t} for thinking@comma{} @samp{-o} for tools).

The Settings column displays the current value of each option (e.g.@comma{} @code{collapsed}@comma{} @code{on}@comma{} @code{off}@comma{} @code{created}@comma{} @code{modified}) highlighted with the @code{transient-value} face@comma{} matching the convention used by @samp{magit} and other transient-based menus.

